<h2 id="false-positive-rates">Measured false-positive rates</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Corpus: @Aibysitter.Web.Linting.RuleMeasurements.CorpusFiles rules files from public GitHub repositories, fetched 2026-10-03: 150 CLAUDE.md, 150 AGENTS.md, 147 GEMINI.md, 126 Copilot instructions, 119 Cursor .mdc, 45 .cursorrules, 18 .windsurfrules. One file per repository per format.</li>
    <li>Sample: up to 30 findings per rule, at most 2 per file, spread across formats. Rules with fewer findings: all of them.</li>
    <li>Two judges: judge A, and judge B, a separate model without access to judge A's verdicts. A finding is a true positive when it is what the rule's summary describes, on text the rule applies to.</li>
    <li>R001, R002, R005, R007 and R013 apply to instructions only. Descriptive prose, pasted documentation and project descriptions are never true positives.</li>
    <li>Ruleset v4 rates are the ruleset v3 sample re-scored for the findings v4 still reports. Rules unchanged since ruleset v2 show their v2 measurement.</li>
    <li>Judge agreement at ruleset v4: 140 of 149 findings (94.0%), Cohen's kappa 0.84.</li>
</ul>
<table class="stack">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Rule</th>
            <th>Judge A</th>
            <th>Judge B</th>
            <th>Sample</th>
            <th>Ruleset</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        @foreach (var id in Aibysitter.Web.Linting.RuleMeasurements.RuleIds)
        {
            var doc = RuleDocs.Find(id)!;
            if (Aibysitter.Web.Linting.RuleMeasurements.Find(id) is { } m)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td><a asp-page="/Rules/Rule" asp-route-id="@id">@id</a> @doc.Name</td>
                    <td>@m.FalsePositivesA of @m.Sample</td>
                    <td>@m.FalsePositivesB of @m.Sample</td>
                    <td>@m.Sample</td>
                    <td>v@(m.Ruleset)</td>
                </tr>
            }
            else
            {
                <tr>
                    <td><a asp-page="/Rules/Rule" asp-route-id="@id">@id</a> @doc.Name</td>
                    <td colspan="4">@Aibysitter.Web.Linting.RuleMeasurements.NotMeasuredReason(id)</td>
                </tr>
            }
        }
    </tbody>
</table>
